{
  "id": "COMPOUND:32416 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Tecleanthine appears to have a shared target relationship with H9, which is a common target of multiple compounds, including Pronuciferine, Scrophuloside B, and Vitetrifolin B. These compounds all direct their activity to Phosphodiesterase 6C, suggesting a potential mechanism where Tecleanthine may exert its effects through a similar pathway. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship between Tecleanthine and Phosphodiesterase 6C, likely through the H9 molecule. The overlapping targets suggest that Tecleanthine may act as a modulator of Phosphodiesterase 6C, potentially by influencing the activity of H9, which in turn affects the enzyme. This integrated evidence supports a mechanism where Tecleanthine could interact with H9 to modulate Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
